{"title":"Career Roadmap · Sonographer","role":"Sonographer","summary":"A Sonographer uses ultrasound equipment to acquire diagnostic images of internal organs, tissues, blood vessels and, depending on training and scope, developing fetuses.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Medical Sonography / Ultrasound Technology"},"about":[{"label":"Important","text":"Sonography is a patient-facing diagnostic imaging profession. The exact scope of practice, supervision, permitted examinations, reporting authority, and registration requirements vary by country and applicable regulations. Students should verify current requirements for the jurisdiction and employer. In India, ultrasound practice is also subject to specific legal and regulatory requirements."}],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Sonographer uses ultrasound equipment to acquire diagnostic images of internal organs, tissues, blood vessels and, depending on training and scope, developing fetuses."},{"type":"h","text":"The role combines:"},{"type":"h","text":"Human anatomy"},{"type":"h","text":"Ultrasound physics"},{"type":"h","text":"Patient care"},{"type":"h","text":"Image acquisition"},{"type":"h","text":"Transducer selection"},{"type":"h","text":"Scanning protocols"},{"type":"h","text":"Doppler techniques"},{"type":"h","text":"Image optimization"},{"type":"h","text":"Clinical documentation"},{"type":"h","text":"Infection control"},{"type":"h","text":"Common areas include:"},{"type":"h","text":"Abdominal sonography"},{"type":"h","text":"Obstetric and gynaecological imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Small-parts imaging"},{"type":"h","text":"Vascular Doppler"},{"type":"h","text":"Musculoskeletal ultrasound"},{"type":"h","text":"Emergency/point-of-care ultrasound support"},{"type":"h","text":"Paediatric imaging"},{"type":"p","text":"A sonographer's primary technical responsibility is gen